// A direct call to a LAZY module's interface prototype — madcmark_parse, which
// <ns_markdown>'s `import madcmark;` serves — beside the fragment's own wrapper.
// Under --std=madc the packed binary binds <ns_markdown> from the pack, so the
// import is replayed, never re-lexed: the restored prototype must carry the
// stamp a live parse gives it (a typed first-call slot against the row's
// spelling), or the call lowers to a direct import of a symbol no library in
// the program provides. The dev binary's live parse of the fragment is the
// oracle: both binaries print the same lines.
int main()
{
    println("available: {}", markdown::available());
    var doc;
    madcmark_parse(&doc, "# Hi\n\ntext\n");
    println("children: {}", php::count(doc["children"]));
    return 0;
}
